{
  "target": "One source-linked formula family slice across catalog/formulas.json, both evaluators, and shared fixtures",
  "scope": "Incrementally expand the Excel 365 formula glossary and bounded Python/Rust evaluator while preserving parity and explicit array-result shapes",
  "context": "Keep the full source inventory distinct from implemented coverage. Preserve source provenance. Use only MIT or Apache-2.0 implementation references and dependencies; do not copy third-party code. Mark profile choices that have not been checked in Excel.",
  "criteria": [
    "Each newly implemented formula has a detailed argument, result, behavior, and source specification",
    "Python and Rust both implement each newly supported formula",
    "The shared corpus covers normal, boundary, and error cases for each new formula, and numeric expected values are grounded in Microsoft examples, independently derived equations, or a high-precision oracle",
    "All shared cases and existing project checks pass in both languages",
    "Every semantic source reference resolves, and implemented counts match catalog status",
    "New implementation sources and dependencies satisfy the MIT or Apache-2.0 rule"
