  "baseline_gates": [
    "The Run 18 accepted candidate has matching Python/Rust conformance fixtures for all 111 implemented functions.",
    "All semantic source references resolve and implemented counts match catalog status.",
    "The complete Python and Rust verification commands pass.",
    "The source-pattern catalog enforces MIT/Apache-only references and no copied code.",
    "New numeric fixtures are checked against a published result, independent derivation, or high-precision oracle; Python/Rust parity alone is not treated as correctness evidence.",
    "Microsoft array/range behavior is source-backed, and local scalar range outputs are not labeled as Excel expected results.",
    "Run 16 preserves Microsoft-documented rules separately from local scalar and numeric profiles for FACT, COMBIN, and COMBINA.",
    "Run 17 preserves those source/profile distinctions for FACTDOUBLE, PERMUT, and PERMUTATIONA and records the mixed-input coercion-before-domain order as a Formula Atlas profile.",
    "Run 18 keeps Microsoft GCD input >= 2^53 and LCM result >= 2^53 boundaries distinct, and identifies both functions as range-capable while labeling scalar range rejection local.",
    "Run 18 labels LCM zero behavior, mixed-input ordering, coercion details, and negative-fraction order as Formula Atlas profiles pending direct Excel validation.",
    "Run 18 uses exact integer fixture comparisons for the 2^53 boundaries; Python/Rust agreement and broad floating tolerance alone do not establish these outputs.",
    "Apache Commons Math ArithmeticUtils is an Apache-2.0 architectural reference only; no code is copied and no dependency is added.",
    "Run 18 accepted GCD and LCM after 57 exact/shared fixtures, independent semantic, parity, and catalog review, all schema/provenance checks, and the full Python/Rust gates; no direct Excel check is claimed.",
    "Run 19 preserves Microsoft-documented SEQUENCE defaults and result-array behavior separately from local dimension coercion, error, and 100000-cell resource profiles; worksheet spill placement remains unsupported.",
    "Run 19 uses only pinned MIT/Apache-2.0 Formualizer v0.7.0 architecture/license references; no source code or runtime dependency is copied.",
    "Rust checks use the checkout-local rust/target directory through CARGO_TARGET_DIR, avoiding Cargo artifacts shared by other checkouts."
